From ba70d42dcaa65a25b526f48f5f0432a027263243 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 17:30:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [BAREBOX] mmu: fix flush_cacheable_pages off-by-one touching guard page

flush_cacheable_pages() accumulates contiguous cacheable page ranges and
tracks flush_end as the exclusive end of each range (i.e. the address
of the first page BEYOND the last cacheable block, which equals the start
address of the next block: the flush_end == addr extension test relies
on this).

When a non-cacheable page (e.g. the stack guard page) creates a gap in
the middle of a flush region followed by more cacheable pages, the code
calls dma_flush_range_end(flush_start, flush_end) just before starting a
new range.  dma_flush_range_end() treats its second argument as an
inclusive end and calls v8_flush_dcache_range(start, end + 1), so the
exclusive flush_end becomes an exclusive bound of end+1.  This causes
dc civac to execute at flush_end itself: the first address of the gap.

On ARMv8 (Cortex-A55/A76), dc civac requires write permission to the VA.
When flush_end equals the guard-page address (MAP_FAULT, no access), the
instruction raises a synchronous Data Abort that barebox's fault handler
reports as "stack overflow" because FAR matches the guard page.

Fix: subtract 1 at both dma_flush_range_end call sites to convert the
exclusive flush_end to the inclusive end that dma_flush_range_end expects.
This keeps the b.lo loop in v8_flush_dcache_range from iterating into the
guard page.

Observed on RK3588S (Radxa CM5) during NVMe/PCIe bring-up.

Signed-off-by: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
---
 arch/arm/cpu/flush_cacheable_pages.h | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/cpu/flush_cacheable_pages.h b/arch/arm/cpu/flush_cacheable_pages.h
index a03e10810d..c46a60071a 100644
--- a/arch/arm/cpu/flush_cacheable_pages.h
+++ b/arch/arm/cpu/flush_cacheable_pages.h
@@ -61,10 +61,14 @@ static void flush_cacheable_pages(void *start, size_t size)
 
 		/*
 		 * We don't have a previous contiguous flush area to append to.
-		 * If we recorded any area before, let's flush it now
+		 * If we recorded any area before, let's flush it now.
+		 * flush_end is the exclusive end of the cacheable range. Subtract
+		 * 1 to convert to the inclusive end expected by dma_flush_range_end,
+		 * preventing dc civac from stepping into the next (possibly fault-mapped)
+		 * page when a non-cacheable page (e.g. the stack guard) follows.
 		 */
 		if (flush_start != ~0UL)
-			dma_flush_range_end(flush_start, flush_end);
+			dma_flush_range_end(flush_start, flush_end - 1);
 
 		/* and start the new contiguous flush area with this page */
 		flush_start = addr;
@@ -73,5 +77,5 @@ static void flush_cacheable_pages(void *start, size_t size)
 
 	/* The previous loop won't flush the last cached range, so do it here */
 	if (flush_start != ~0UL)
-		dma_flush_range_end(flush_start, flush_end);
+		dma_flush_range_end(flush_start, flush_end - 1);
 }
